&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Shift Schedule&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1st Shift:&lt;/strong&gt; Monday–Friday, 6:00 AM–2:30 PM (8-hour shifts)&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Assembly &amp;amp; Test Technician I–IV&lt;/strong&gt; supports the hands-on assembly, integration, inspection, testing, troubleshooting, and manufacturing execution of mechanical and electromechanical sub-assemblies used in large-format laser powder bed fusion (LPBF) 3D printers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role works closely with Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Supply Chain, Operations, and other technicians to translate engineering requirements into high-quality physical hardware and repeatable manufacturing execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position may be filled at the &lt;strong&gt;Technician I, II, III, or IV level&lt;/strong&gt; based on demonstrated knowledge, experience, technical capability, independence, complexity of work, and technical leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Assembly &amp;amp; Integration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assemble and integrate mechanical and electromechanical LPBF printer sub-assemblies using engineering drawings, BOMs, specifications, travelers, and work instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Install mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, fluid, motion, sensor, wiring, harness, and related hardware as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform precision fastening, torqueing, alignment, leveling, measurement, and dimensional verification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify hardware configuration, workmanship, critical characteristics, and dimensional requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify missing, damaged, incorrect, or improperly configured components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify potential fit, form, function, manufacturability, accessibility, tooling, or integration concerns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect precision, high-value, and high-surface-finish components from damage or contamination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Supply Chain, Operations, and other technicians to meet production priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance and support to other technicians as appropriate to level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Testing &amp;amp; Verification&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform functional and acceptance testing of completed sub-assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, pressure, leak, motion, and other applicable subsystem tests.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Configure and operate test equipment, fixtures, and instrumentation appropriate to the work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate test results against engineering requirements and acceptance criteria.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify abnormal conditions and communicate test results, observations, and hardware behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot test failures at a complexity appropriate to experience and level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify hardware performance following adjustment, rework, or corrective action.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare verified sub-assemblies for downstream printer integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Troubleshooting &amp;amp; Rework&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply structured troubleshooting methods to mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, and electromechanical hardware issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use measurements, observations, test data, configuration information, and physical evidence to investigate failure modes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform approved rework, adjustment, repair, alignment, and corrective-action activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Determine when issues can be resolved within established processes and when Engineering or additional technical support is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support root-cause investigation and resolution of hardware, process, component, and workmanship issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clearly communicate troubleshooting observations, findings, and corrective actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support other technicians during troubleshooting and rework activities as appropriate to level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;ERP &amp;amp; Production Documentation&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use ERP and manufacturing systems to record work orders, material consumption, completed operations, rework, inspection, test activity, and production status.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate hardware configuration, serialized-part, revision, and traceability records as applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete travelers, build records, inspection results, and test documentation accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify discrepancies between physical hardware, engineering configuration, manufacturing processes, and production records.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain alignment between as-built hardware and manufacturing documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Manufacturing Improvement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve assembly sequence, tooling, accessibility, test setup, quality, repeatability, safety, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide practical feedback to Engineering and Manufacturing Engineering based on hands-on hardware experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and improvement of work instructions, travelers, standard work, tooling, fixtures, and test methods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support implementation of engineering and process changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to transitioning new or evolving hardware into repeatable manufacturing execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote consistent workmanship, configuration control, documentation, traceability, and adherence to engineering requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support training and knowledge sharing across the technician team as appropriate to level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant hands-on experience in mechanical assembly, electromechanical integration, manufacturing, equipment build, testing, or a related technical field appropriate to the level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical aptitude and ability to safely use hand tools, power tools, torque tools, and measurement equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret engineering drawings, BOMs, specifications, travelers, schematics, and controlled technical documentation appropriate to the level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience performing mechanical and/or electromechanical assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform functional testing and troubleshoot hardware issues at a complexity appropriate to the level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to quality and workmanship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to accurately document work and maintain production and hardware traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic computer skills and ability to use or learn ERP, MRP, MES, or similar manufacturing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to collaborate effectively with technicians and cross-functional teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with the level of independence appropriate to the position.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with industrial 3D printers, additive manufacturing, or complex capital equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with laser powder bed fusion (LPBF) systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in aerospace, automotive, robotics, semiconductor, precision manufacturing, or similar industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with motion systems, precision mechanisms, motors, sensors, pneumatics, machine controls, vacuum, pressure, or fluid systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical assembly, wiring, harness, or electrical troubleshooting experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pressure, leak, electrical, or functional testing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with precision alignment, GD&amp;amp;T, or advanced measurement techniques.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with serialized or revision-controlled hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Lean, continuous improvement, or manufacturing process development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing assembly or test procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully onsite manufacturing and development environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent interaction with Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Supply Chain, and Operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular standing, walking, bending, reaching, and working around large equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move up to 50 pounds independently; heavier components require assistance or lifting equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May work around electrical, pneumatic, mechanical, and other industrial systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires adherence to PPE, ESD, safety, cleanliness, and manufacturing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May require extended hours or occasional weekend support based on production priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
