&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$133,766&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,977 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Divergent Technologies is seeking an Integrated Assembly Technician to join our Production Department. This position plays a vital role in assembling, fitting, and finalizing complex additively manufactured metal components used in our advanced aerospace, defense, and automotive structures. The ideal candidate has hands-on experience in precision assembly, mechanical fitting, and inspection, with a focus on achieving world-class quality standards in a fast-paced production environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Assembly and Fitment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assemble structural and mechanical components following engineering drawings, specifications, and work instructions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align, fit, and secure parts using mechanical fasteners, adhesives, or joining techniques appropriate for additively manufactured metal assemblies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform dry fits and verification checks before final installation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure precise alignment and optimal fit.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality and Inspection&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect sub-assemblies and final assemblies for dimensional accuracy, cosmetic finish, and mechanical integrity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform leak down testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify any defects or inconsistencies, escalating issues when necessary.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain detailed documentation of measurements, inspection data, and process steps.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tooling and Equipment&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safely operate hand tools, torque tools, pneumatic systems, and precision measuring instruments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and calibrate tools as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in fixture setup and basic troubleshooting of tools.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration and Communication&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with production, machining, and finishing teams to ensure smooth workflow and component compatibility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate effectively with engineers and supervisors regarding technical issues or design feedback.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Safety and Compliance&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow all safety protocols, personal protective equipment (PPE) requirements, and environmental guidelines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain a clean, organized work area consistent with 5S and Lean Manufacturing principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated proficiency in mechanical assembly, precision fitting, or related manufacturing roles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with keysert locking inserts, helicoils and taps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiar with helicoil specs and size specifications.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of lubricants and sealants used in the aerospace field.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Thorough understanding of “wet” and “dry” insert installation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to read and interpret technical drawings, blueprints, and assembly instructions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with torque specifications, fastener types, and mechanical alignment procedures.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and commitment to quality workmanship.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High school diploma or equivalent required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience assembling metallic and composite components in the automotive, aerospace, or additive manufacturing industries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of GD&amp;amp;T (Geometric Dimensioning and Tolerancing).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with post-processing environments (heat treatment, finishing, or coating operations).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Basic computer literacy for CAD (Siemens NX), MES, documentation, and ERP system updates.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong desire to learn new skills and grow, utilizing down time as an opportunity to gain new abilities and attributes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performed in a manufacturing environment with exposure to noise and machinery&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Requires frequent standing, walking, bending, reaching, and handling of precision tools and materials.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be able to lift up to 40 lbs. independently and 50 lbs. with assistance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May involve crouching, climbing, confined spaces, or work at heights.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PPE (including but not limited to safety glasses, hearing protection, gloves, respirators as needed) and company uniform are required.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;May occasionally require extended or weekend hours to meet production deadlines.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Divergent, our pay range is based on the level of the job. For this role, we will consider candidates at T03 level as evaluated through our interview process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;T03/ Technician 3: $36.00 - $50.00&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$36&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$50 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Integration Technician II–III&lt;/strong&gt; is responsible for the hands-on integration of large-format laser powder bed fusion (LPBF) printers within the Machine Development Operations department. Working from completed sub-assemblies produced by the Sub-Assembly work center and the printer integration hardware BOM, this role brings together mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, inert-gas, motion, powder-handling, and other system-level hardware to build complete printer platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The technician executes printer integration activities primarily through MES work order instructions, supported by engineering drawings, specifications, BOMs, controlled documents, and applicable change-management systems. The role performs precise installation, alignment, fastening, routing, connection, verification, troubleshooting, and rework while maintaining configuration control, traceability, workmanship, and build quality.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of the Long Beach factory launch and ramp, the Integration Technician works with Design Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Sub-Assembly, Supply Chain, and Operations to resolve integration challenges and improve the build process. The role provides hands-on feedback that supports repeatable work instructions, standard work, tooling, fixtures, and integration practices.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position may be filled at the &lt;strong&gt;Technician II or Technician III level&lt;/strong&gt; based on demonstrated knowledge, experience, technical capability, independence, complexity of work, and technical leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Printer Integration&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Execute MES work order instructions to integrate complete large-format LPBF printers from completed sub-assemblies and integration hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow released work instructions, BOMs, drawings, specifications, and controlling documents to perform installation, fastening, torqueing, routing, alignment, adjustment, and connection activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Integrate mechanical structures, electrical systems, pneumatics, inert-gas systems, powder handling, motion systems, sensing, controls, and other printer interfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and verify interfaces between major sub-assemblies, structures, modules, and components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform precision mechanical and electromechanical assembly using calibrated torque tools, hand tools, power tools, and precision measurement equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify alignment, clearances, fits, mounting conditions, hardware identification, orientation, configuration, and installation requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Route cables, tubing, hoses, harnesses, and other system interfaces; install and connect sensors, actuators, motors, drives, electrical components, and pneumatic hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform required dimensional, alignment, torque, installation, and workmanship verification and maintain accurate as-built configuration and traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Equipment &amp;amp; Material Handling&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use approved cranes, forklifts, telehandlers, hoists, lifting fixtures, and other material-handling equipment to position and install large or heavy assemblies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safely rig, move, position, and install assemblies using approved equipment and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow applicable rigging, lifting, LOTO, machine-safety, and material-handling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Troubleshooting &amp;amp; Rework&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot mechanical, electromechanical, pneumatic, motion, and system-interface integration issues at a complexity appropriate to experience and level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose alignment, fit, tolerance, interference, routing, component-interface, installation-sequence, and configuration issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform approved repair, rework, adjustment, replacement, and corrective activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify discrepancies between released requirements and as-built conditions and escalate issues requiring Engineering evaluation, disposition, or clarification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support Engineering with root-cause analysis, corrective actions, engineering changes, deviations, nonconformances, and configuration-management activities as appropriate to level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify hardware and integration work following corrective actions, repair, rework, or adjustment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Manufacturing Documentation &amp;amp; Configuration Control&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete MES work orders, digital travelers, checklists, inspection records, and other required manufacturing documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use applicable engineering change, deviation, nonconformance, and configuration-management systems to document and control changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verify integration work against MES instructions, drawings, BOMs, specifications, acceptance criteria, and configuration requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate as-built configuration, hardware identification, revision control, and traceability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Manufacturing &amp;amp; Process Improvement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps, errors, ambiguities, or impractical steps within MES work instructions and supporting documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide hands-on technical feedback to Manufacturing and Design Engineering to improve MES work instructions, standard work, checklists, and integration procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring integration issues and opportunities to improve build sequence, tooling, fixtures, material presentation, workstation layout, and integration flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Manufacturing and Design Engineering to improve buildability, accessibility, manufacturability, quality, and repeatability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support factory installation, commissioning, qualification, process development, and printer build-ramp activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify constraints affecting build schedule, quality, or repeatability and support resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Team &amp;amp; Cross-Functional Support&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Sub-Assembly, Design Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Quality, Supply Chain, and Operations to communicate technical issues, material constraints, build status, and integration risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with other technicians during complex or unfamiliar integration activities and provide technical guidance as appropriate to level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support safe, repeatable, and scalable printer integration practices as factory operations ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain clean, organized, FOD-controlled work areas and follow applicable safety, workmanship, ESD, LOTO, rigging, and material-handling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2+ years of hands-on mechanical/electromechanical assembly, equipment integration, manufacturing, or related technical experience; equivalent experience considered.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with complex mechanical, electromechanical, industrial, or capital equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to interpret engineering drawings, BOMs, specifications, schematics, and technical work instructions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of mechanical interfaces, fasteners, torque, alignment, fits, clearances, tolerances, and precision assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using calibrated torque tools, hand tools, power tools, and precision measurement equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mechanical and electromechanical troubleshooting skills appropriate to the level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large or heavy assemblies and approved cranes, forklifts, telehandlers, hoists, or similar equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to safely rig, move, position, and install large or heavy assemblies using approved equipment and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within controlled manufacturing, configuration-management, and revision-controlled processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using MES, ERP, work-order, or digital manufacturing systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently on integration activities while collaborating effectively with technicians, Engineering, Quality, and Manufacturing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-format industrial equipment, automation, robotics, or complex machinery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with additive manufacturing or LPBF systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mechanical, electrical, pneumatic, hydraulic, inert-gas, motion, controls, sensing, or powder-handling systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with precision alignment, dimensional inspection, GD&amp;amp;T, or tolerance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with multi-level BOMs and serialized or revision-controlled hardware.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or improving MES work instructions, standard work, tooling, fixtures, or manufacturing processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting NPI, prototype development, commissioning, qualification, production ramp, or factory launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aerospace, defense, automotive, robotics, semiconductor, or other high-reliability manufacturing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with root-cause analysis, corrective action, Lean, 5S, or continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Qualification or prior experience operating overhead cranes, forklifts, telehandlers, or similar equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;1st or 2nd shift&lt;/strong&gt; based on business and manufacturing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully onsite in Long Beach, CA, in an active factory development environment involving construction, equipment installation, commissioning, process development, and facility modifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work around large-format machinery, robotics, electrical systems, motion systems, powder, inert gas, and industrial equipment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular use of overhead cranes, forklifts, telehandlers, hoists, and lifting fixtures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent standing, walking, bending, reaching, kneeling, climbing, and hands-on assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move up to 50 lb independently; heavier loads require approved equipment, assistance, or team lifting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Follow applicable FOD, ESD, LOTO, rigging, lifting, machine safety, construction-site, and material-handling requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended hours, overtime, and weekend work may be required during factory ramp, builds, commissioning, qualification, and production activities. Pasted text&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Divergent, our pay range is based on the level of the job. For this role, we will consider candidates at levels&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;T02 - T03&lt;/strong&gt; as evaluated through our interview process.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T02 / Technician II:&lt;/strong&gt; $31 - $43 per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;T03 / Technician III:&lt;/strong&gt; $36 - $50 per hour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
