&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;Lead planning and execution of factory electrical infrastructure and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SpellingErrorV2Themed SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;workcenter&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt; buildouts that translate production requirements into operational manufacturing space. &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;be responsible for&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt; driving owner-side electrical infrastructure planning, coordinating utility service and distribution upgrades, and leading technical execution of electrical infrastructure projects supporting factory development and manufacturing equipment deployment. This role requires strong electrical engineering &lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;expertise&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot;&gt;, cross-functional problem-solving, and the ability to make day-to-day technical decisions that keep projects aligned with production goals, schedules, and budgets.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP Selected SCXW237130685 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical Supply &amp;amp; Capacity Planning: Lead planning and execution of factory electrical supply strategies by evaluating current and future power demand, utility service capacity, and infrastructure requirements supporting manufacturing growth. Serve as the primary owner-side engineering interface with utility providers to coordinate service upgrades, line extensions, infrastructure requirements, and energization schedules. Partner with external A&amp;amp;E firms to evaluate phased power delivery strategies and alternative supply solutions considering cost, schedule, reliability, technical risk, and long-term scalability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Factory Electrical Distribution: Lead planning and technical execution of factory electrical distribution infrastructure, including medium- and low-voltage systems, transformers, switchgear, switchboards, panelboards, feeders, and equipment power connections. Define electrical infrastructure requirements, evaluate distribution capacity, and review A&amp;amp;E-developed designs for alignment with factory requirements, applicable codes, constructability, reliability, and scalability. Coordinate with A&amp;amp;E partners, electrical contractors, and equipment vendors to ensure distribution systems support manufacturing equipment deployment and future factory expansion.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical Engineering &amp;amp; Equipment Integration: Lead owner-side electrical engineering coordination from initial concept development through construction and equipment commissioning. Establish electrical infrastructure requirements and review engineering deliverables prepared by external A&amp;amp;E partners, including load calculations, single-line diagrams, power distribution plans, grounding requirements, equipment specifications, and electrical system studies. Evaluate equipment interfaces, facility hookup requirements, and infrastructure constraints to develop practical solutions supporting manufacturing readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data &amp;amp; IT Infrastructure: Lead planning and cross-functional coordination of factory data and IT infrastructure supporting manufacturing operations and equipment deployment. Partner with IT stakeholders, engineering teams, and equipment vendors to define infrastructure requirements, resolve integration constraints, and ensure alignment with factory development plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Factory Controls &amp;amp; Automation: Lead planning and technical coordination of facility controls and automation infrastructure supporting manufacturing operations. Partner with controls engineering, IT, facilities, and equipment vendors to establish system requirements, resolve technical interfaces, and coordinate integration into factory infrastructure and construction plans.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electrical Construction &amp;amp; Installation: Lead technical coordination for electrical infrastructure, construction, and equipment installation activities by serving as the primary engineering point of contact for electrical scope, infrastructure requirements, and equipment integration. Review contractor submittals, vendor shop drawings, and technical RFIs to verify alignment with engineering requirements and drive resolution of technical issues. Partner with construction coordinators, facilities teams, contractors, and vendors to resolve field constraints, support construction sequencing, and drive electrical testing, commissioning, and energization readiness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Factory &amp;amp; Work Center Buildout Planning: Lead development and execution of factory and workcenter buildout strategies by defining and optimizing equipment integration strategies, infrastructure requirements, and deployment solutions while reviewing factory layouts and assessing manufacturing and facility constraints. Lead technical coordination across engineering, procurement, operations, and facilities stakeholders to establish deployment strategies that support manufacturing capacity planning, operational efficiency, safety, production ramp timelines, and long-term scalability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project Schedule Ownership &amp;amp; Capital Project Coordination: Drive technical execution strategy, deployment schedule alignment, and critical path coordination for factory development initiatives by proactively identifying infrastructure dependencies, integration risks, and manufacturing readiness gaps. Lead technical evaluations of capital infrastructure alternatives considering scope, cost, schedule, performance, and scalability. Support project scope development, budget planning, contractor proposals, and procurement activities while driving corrective actions required to maintain execution alignment with production objectives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Engineering &amp;amp; Continuous Improvement: Lead cross-functional technical coordination across engineering, operations, facilities, supply chain, contractors, OEM vendors, and external partners to resolve complex engineering challenges and maintain alignment across factory development activities. Develop and maintain factory configuration records, infrastructure standards, technical requirements, and deployment documentation. Capture lessons learned and drive continuous improvement initiatives focused on engineering execution, infrastructure planning, deployment consistency, and repeatable factory development methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering or a closely related technical discipline.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335557856&amp;quot;:16777215,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;7+ years of electrical engineering experience supporting manufacturing facilities, industrial infrastructure, electrical power distribution, or capital project execution.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strong technical understanding of medium- and low-voltage electrical distribution systems, including transformers, switchgear, switchboards, panelboards, feeders, and industrial equipment power requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience developing requirements for and reviewing electrical engineering deliverables, including single-line diagrams, load calculations, power distribution plans, equipment specifications, and electrical system studies.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience supporting electrical infrastructure planning, construction coordination, equipment installation, commissioning, or utility infrastructure upgrades.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Working knowledge of applicable electrical codes and safety requirements, including NEC, NFPA 70E, and relevant electrical engineering standards.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to independently evaluate complex engineering problems, develop technical solutions, and drive implementation across multiple projects and stakeholders.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Experience coordinating technical workstreams across engineering disciplines, A&amp;amp;E partners, contractors, utilities, and equipment vendors.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Strong organizational and communication skills with the ability to manage multiple parallel engineering activities, technical decisions, and project priorities.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Ability to develop and maintain clear technical documentation, engineering requirements, configuration records, and project deliverables.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
