&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-teams=&quot;true&quot;&gt;The Senior Employee Relations Specialist is a key architect of how Divergent builds a fair, high-performing workplace as we scale. Combining deep employee relations expertise with strong judgment, operational rigor, and a builder mindset, this role will navigate complex workplace matters, strengthen manager capability, and translate employee insights into better policies, practices, and organizational decisions. From resolving sensitive employee matters to building the systems and programs that shape the employee experience, this role offers the opportunity to make a visible impact on both our people and the organization.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Employee Relations &amp;amp; Workplace Support
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a primary point of contact for managers and employees regarding employee relations concerns, workplace issues, policy interpretation, and employee experience matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct Tier 1 and Tier 2 employee relations intake, investigations, fact-finding, documentation, and resolution recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with managers to address employee concerns, performance-related matters, workplace conflicts, and policy-related questions in a consistent and compliant manner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with People leadership and Legal on complex, sensitive, or high-risk employee relations matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and organized employee relations documentation, investigation records, and case files.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify employee relations trends and recommend proactive solutions that improve employee experience and reduce organizational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support consistent application of company policies, procedures, and workplace practices across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and continuously improve employee relations systems, workflows, documentation standards, intake processes, and escalation frameworks that improve consistency, visibility, and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leave, Accommodations &amp;amp; Workplace Compliance
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer Leave of Absence programs, including employee communications, documentation management, case tracking, and return-to-work coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate workplace accommodations and interactive process activities in partnership with employees, managers, healthcare providers, and external vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support workers&#39; compensation administration, claim coordination, return-to-work planning, and documentation management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate immigration case administration and partnership with external immigration counsel and vendors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor assigned compliance programs and ensure accurate documentation, process adherence, and timely follow-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Policy Governance, Organizational Health &amp;amp; Operational Scalability
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify policy gaps, workplace trends, organizational risks, and opportunities to improve employee experience and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Draft, maintain, and implement People policies, procedures, and operational guidelines in partnership with People leadership, Legal, and business stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support policy communication, training, and change management efforts to promote consistent application across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop systems, reporting, and organizational health insights that improve visibility into employee relations activity, compliance programs, workplace trends, and operational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and maintain self-service resources, SOPs, process documentation, workflow tools, and knowledge resources that improve consistency, scalability, and manager/employee enablement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement process improvements that enhance operational efficiency, organizational effectiveness, and employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Legal, Payroll, Finance, Security, Talent Acquisition, and business leaders to support employee experience and workplace compliance initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build trusted working relationships with managers and leaders across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support organizational initiatives and projects that improve People Operations effectiveness and employee experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence stakeholders through data, process recommendations, and operational insights that improve organizational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience independently managing employee relations matters, workplace investigations, and employee support programs while exercising sound judgment and discretion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying California employment practices and workplace compliance requirements in the administration of employee relations, leave, accommodations, and related workplace programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting employee relations intake, investigations, fact-finding, documentation, and case management activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering leave of absence, workplace accommodations, workers&#39; compensation, or similar employee programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with Legal on employee relations, workplace investigations, accommodations, leave administration, or compliance matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated judgment in interpreting and applying policies, procedures, and workplace practices while balancing employee experience, business needs, and organizational risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying operational challenges and improving processes, workflows, systems, or documentation to enhance consistency, scalability, and organizational effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building, analytical, communication, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professionalism and discretion when handling sensitive and confidential employee matters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to perform the essential functions of the position in a standard office environment, including extended periods of computer-based work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to move throughout company facilities and/or transport light materials as needed to support business activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting multi-state employee populations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience utilizing HRIS systems, case management platforms, Jira, Power BI, workflow tools, or similar operational technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing dashboards, operational reporting, workforce insights, or organizational health metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using data and trend analysis to identify risks, inform decision-making, or drive process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with immigration administration and vendor coordination.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Organizational Psychology, Analytics, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This role will be based onsite in our Torrance, CA headquarters and will ultimately relocate to our Long Beach, CA facility.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fast-paced, highly collaborative environment supporting a rapidly scaling organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant cross-functional interaction with managers, employees, leadership, and external partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to influence both employee experience and the operational infrastructure that enables organizational growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;At Divergent, our pay range is based on the level of the job. For this role, we will consider candidates at level S05 as evaluated through our interview process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 0, 0);&quot;&gt;Senior Employee Relations Specialist/ S05: $109,240 - $150,210&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$109,240&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,210 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Join our mission to redefine aerospace and automotive manufacturing through advanced Additive Manufacturing. We are seeking a&amp;nbsp;hands-on&amp;nbsp;Additive Manufacturing Equipment Engineer to&amp;nbsp;help&amp;nbsp;transition&amp;nbsp;next-generation Laser Powder Bed Fusion (L-PBF) production equipment from development into high-volume manufacturing.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;This role&amp;nbsp;helps ensure&amp;nbsp;our production equipment is stable, reliable, scalable, and capable of delivering world-class safety, quality, delivery, and cost performance. As our manufacturing footprint expands across multiple factories, you will solve&amp;nbsp;equipment&amp;nbsp;problems&amp;nbsp;at the machine level&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;help&amp;nbsp;transform those solutions into engineering standards deployed across the entire fleet.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Success in this role requires&amp;nbsp;strong&amp;nbsp;troubleshooting skills,&amp;nbsp;independent technical&amp;nbsp;judgment, and the&amp;nbsp;drive&amp;nbsp;to&amp;nbsp;grow into broader fleet-level ownership. You will work alongside senior&amp;nbsp;equipment&amp;nbsp;engineers to stabilize new machines, improve reliability, and&amp;nbsp;build&amp;nbsp;the&amp;nbsp;standards that carry the fleet as it scales.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Equipment Engineer-Electrical, you will be a subject matter expert on the electrical systems of production L-PBF equipment, including power distribution, control circuits, sensors and instrumentation, wiring, drives, and safety interlocks. You will own technical issues and projects on your assigned equipment, set the approach and standards for recurring technical challenges, and work across Equipment Engineering, Service, Operations, Quality, and Development Engineering. You will mentor technicians and peers. The Equipment Engineering team focuses on the three areas below, and you will contribute to all of them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;You will:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:120}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Support Service and Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing work instructions and write new ones where gaps exist, with the goal of Service team autonomy for most day-to-day issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical resource for operators and Service, including formally as part of the Service Level Agreement (SLA). This includes support for novel issues that existing procedures do not cover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preventative maintenance improvements based on observed equipment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor technicians and operators so that knowledge from difficult investigations moves out of individuals and into the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Own Equipment Reliability and Resolve Fleet Problems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take technical ownership of assigned equipment after qualification, and track performance against safety, quality, delivery, and cost baselines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot electrical issues on L-PBF equipment, such as power distribution and high-power subsystems, control circuits, sensors and instrumentation, wiring and harnesses, drives and motors, and safety interlocks, and work with mechanical and controls engineers when a failure crosses those boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mine existing datasets to discover issues, in particular machine process data and downstream printed part data (non-conformances, witness coupons), and connect the two to find causes that neither dataset shows alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to trend and reliability data across the fleet, and use it to prioritize your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and complete RCCAs end to end: identify the issue, set short-term containment, and drive long-term corrective action. Own investigations on your equipment and in your domain, and support cross-functional investigations led by others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Development Engineering: provide regular input on machine reliability and recommend targeted fixes with input from Operations and Service. Prioritized requests to the Development organization are an output of the team, not of one person, and you will contribute your domain expertise to the team&#39;s priority list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cost reduction through equipment optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Change and Configuration Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help determine when and where specific changes to assets are made, and apply the team&#39;s guidance on what does and does not need formal change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support improvements to both the change approval process and the configuration control process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document lessons learned so they can be standardized across the fleet and future factories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in manufacturing engineering, equipment engineering, reliability engineering, or advanced production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning the sustaining performance of production equipment and supporting it through launch or ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong electrical troubleshooting skill on production equipment (for example power, control circuits, sensors, and instrumentation), including reading schematics and one-line diagrams, with working knowledge of mechanical systems sufficient to troubleshoot alongside mechanical engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead root cause investigations using structured methodologies (e.g., RCCA, 5 Whys, Fishbone, Fault Tree) on recurring or ambiguous problems, and to verify that corrective actions held.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and data-driven decision-making skills, including finding problems in large datasets and not only responding to reported failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work and influence across engineering, operations, quality, maintenance, and service teams without direct authority, and to communicate clearly with people at very different levels of technical depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or training other engineers or technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Laser Powder Bed Fusion (L-PBF) or other metal additive manufacturing technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electrical subsystems common to L-PBF and similar equipment, such as laser and high-power systems, heaters, motion drives, sensors and data acquisition (DAQ), or safety interlocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with electrical safety practices (for example NFPA 70E and LOTO).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to a fleet-level reliability, trending, or performance program (for example OEE, MTBF/MTTR, or failure-mode tracking) across multiple machines or sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing or standardizing work instructions that enabled a Service or Operations team to work more independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a configuration management or engineering change process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with machine sensor data or manufacturing analytics (for example SQL, Python, or similar tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with controls systems, PLCs, industrial automation, or machine integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting capital equipment installation, commissioning, or factory expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AS9100, AMS, PPAP, APQP, or equivalent quality systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Divergent, our pay range is based on the level of the job. For this role, we will consider candidates at levels E04 - E06 as evaluated through our interview process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer II / E04: $111,300 - $153,040&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sr. Engineer / E05: $128,520 - $176,720&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff Engineer / E06: 148,430 - 204,090&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$111,300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$176,720 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Senior Equipment Engineer-Mechanical, you will be a subject matter expert on the mechanical systems of production L-PBF equipment, including motion, recoating, and build platform systems, inert gas flow and filtration, cooling and thermal management, and powder handling. You will own technical issues and projects on your assigned equipment, set the approach and standards for recurring technical challenges, and work across Equipment Engineering, Service, Operations, Quality, and Development Engineering. You will mentor technicians and peers. The Equipment Engineering team focuses on the three areas below, and you will contribute to all of them.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Support Service and Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve existing work instructions and write new ones where gaps exist, with the goal of Service team autonomy for most day-to-day issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as a technical resource for operators and Service, including formally as part of the Service Level Agreement (SLA). This includes support for novel issues that existing procedures do not cover.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support preventative maintenance improvements based on observed equipment performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor technicians and operators so that knowledge from difficult investigations moves out of individuals and into the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Own Equipment Reliability and Resolve Fleet Problems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take technical ownership of assigned equipment after qualification, and track performance against safety, quality, delivery, and cost baselines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot mechanical issues on L-PBF equipment, such as recoater and build platform performance, motion and alignment, wear and tolerance stack-up, gas flow and filtration, cooling, and powder handling, and work with electrical and controls engineers when a failure crosses those boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mine existing datasets to discover issues, in particular machine process data and downstream printed part data (non-conformances, witness coupons), and connect the two to find causes that neither dataset shows alone.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to trend and reliability data across the fleet, and use it to prioritize your work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Initiate and complete RCCAs end to end: identify the issue, set short-term containment, and drive long-term corrective action. Own investigations on your equipment and in your domain, and support cross-functional investigations led by others.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engage with Development Engineering: provide regular input on machine reliability and recommend targeted fixes with input from Operations and Service. Prioritized requests to the Development organization are an output of the team, not of one person, and you will contribute your domain expertise to the team&#39;s priority list.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cost reduction through equipment optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt; Change and Configuration Management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help determine when and where specific changes to assets are made, and apply the team&#39;s guidance on what does and does not need formal change control.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support improvements to both the change approval process and the configuration control process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document lessons learned so they can be standardized across the fleet and future factories.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical approach for assigned projects, and give clear, data-backed recommendations to management on tradeoffs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support installation, commissioning, FAT/SAT, qualification, and production readiness for new equipment and factory expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support quality compliance (AS9100, AMS, PPAP) and the analysis of equipment-related quality issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide input on Design for Manufacturability (DFM) and Design for Reliability (DFR) for next-generation machines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Mechanical Engineering, Manufacturing Engineering, Mechatronics, or a related discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in manufacturing engineering, equipment engineering, reliability engineering, or advanced production environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning the sustaining performance of production equipment and supporting it through launch or ramp.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong mechanical troubleshooting skill on production equipment (for example motion, fluid, gas, or thermal systems), with working knowledge of electrical and controls systems sufficient to troubleshoot alongside electrical and controls engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead root cause investigations using structured methodologies (e.g., RCCA, 5 Whys, Fishbone, Fault Tree) on recurring or ambiguous problems, and to verify that corrective actions held.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and data-driven decision-making skills, including finding problems in large datasets and not only responding to reported failures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work and influence across engineering, operations, quality, maintenance, and service teams without direct authority, and to communicate clearly with people at very different levels of technical depth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience mentoring or training other engineers or technicians.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Laser Powder Bed Fusion (L-PBF) or other metal additive manufacturing technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with mechanical subsystems common to L-PBF and similar equipment, such as recoating or powder handling, precision motion and alignment, inert gas flow and filtration, chillers and thermal management, or vacuum and pressure systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GD&amp;amp;T, tolerance analysis, and CAD (for example SolidWorks), and with reading mechanical drawings and P&amp;amp;IDs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to a fleet-level reliability, trending, or performance program (for example OEE, MTBF/MTTR, or failure-mode tracking) across multiple machines or sites.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience writing or standardizing work instructions that enabled a Service or Operations team to work more independently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a configuration management or engineering change process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with machine sensor data or manufacturing analytics (for example SQL, Python, or similar tools).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with controls systems, PLCs, industrial automation, or machine integration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting capital equipment installation, commissioning, or factory expansion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of AS9100, AMS, PPAP, APQP, or equivalent quality systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Divergent, our pay range is based on the level of the job. For this role, we will consider candidates at levels E04 - E06 as evaluated through our interview process.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engineer II / E04: $111,300 - $153,040&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sr. Engineer / E05: $128,520 - $176,720&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Staff Engineer / E06: 148,430 - 204,090&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$111,300&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$176,720 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;1631&quot; data-end=&quot;1641&quot;&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;1643&quot; data-end=&quot;2038&quot;&gt;Divergent is seeking a &lt;strong data-start=&quot;1666&quot; data-end=&quot;1705&quot;&gt;Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; to develop and scale software systems that power the next generation of digital manufacturing. This role is ideal for an engineer who thrives on solving complex technical challenges, driving architectural decisions, and delivering business-critical applications across engineering, manufacturing, and factory operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;2040&quot; data-end=&quot;2438&quot;&gt;As a Senior Engineer, you will own large-scale initiatives from concept through deployment, influence technical strategy, mentor other engineers, and collaborate across disciplines to deliver highly reliable and scalable software platforms. You will operate with significant autonomy and play a key role in advancing the software ecosystem that enables Divergent&#39;s automated manufacturing platform.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;2445&quot; data-end=&quot;2456&quot;&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;2997&quot; data-end=&quot;3035&quot;&gt;Full-Stack Application Development&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3037&quot; data-end=&quot;3469&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3037&quot; data-end=&quot;3159&quot;&gt;Design, build, and maintain production-grade applications using TypeScript, Node.js, React, and modern web technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3160&quot; data-end=&quot;3255&quot;&gt;Develop robust APIs, services, and user experiences that support critical business functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3256&quot; data-end=&quot;3366&quot;&gt;Deliver complex features and systems from requirements gathering through deployment and operational support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3367&quot; data-end=&quot;3469&quot;&gt;Optimize application performance, reliability, and user experience across the full technology stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;3471&quot; data-end=&quot;3509&quot;&gt;Data Architecture &amp;amp; Systems Design&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3511&quot; data-end=&quot;3839&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3511&quot; data-end=&quot;3630&quot;&gt;Design and evolve relational and NoSQL data models supporting large-scale manufacturing and engineering applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3631&quot; data-end=&quot;3736&quot;&gt;Develop scalable data architectures that enable analytics, automation, and operational decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3737&quot; data-end=&quot;3839&quot;&gt;Ensure system integrity, security, performance, and maintainability across distributed environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;3841&quot; data-end=&quot;3868&quot;&gt;Cross-Functional Impact&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;3870&quot; data-end=&quot;4247&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3870&quot; data-end=&quot;3995&quot;&gt;Collaborate closely with Product Management, Manufacturing Engineering, Robotics, Design Engineering, and Operations teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;3996&quot; data-end=&quot;4072&quot;&gt;Translate complex business requirements into scalable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4073&quot; data-end=&quot;4152&quot;&gt;Serve as a trusted technical advisor to stakeholders across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4153&quot; data-end=&quot;4247&quot;&gt;Lead technical discussions and influence decision-making across multiple teams and projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3 data-start=&quot;4249&quot; data-end=&quot;4288&quot;&gt;Mentorship &amp;amp; Engineering Excellence&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;4290&quot; data-end=&quot;4687&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4290&quot; data-end=&quot;4403&quot;&gt;Mentor and develop junior and mid-level engineers through technical guidance, code reviews, and design reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4404&quot; data-end=&quot;4507&quot;&gt;Promote engineering best practices, software quality, testing strategies, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4508&quot; data-end=&quot;4613&quot;&gt;Drive continuous improvement initiatives across development processes, tooling, and team effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4614&quot; data-end=&quot;4687&quot;&gt;Foster a culture of collaboration, ownership, and technical excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;4694&quot; data-end=&quot;4717&quot;&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;4719&quot; data-end=&quot;5669&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4719&quot; data-end=&quot;4807&quot;&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology subject to U.S. export controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4808&quot; data-end=&quot;4959&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Computer Engineering, or related discipline; equivalent practical experience considered.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;4960&quot; data-end=&quot;5076&quot;&gt;8+ years of professional software engineering experience, including significant full-stack development experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5077&quot; data-end=&quot;5130&quot;&gt;Expert-level proficiency in TypeScript and Node.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5131&quot; data-end=&quot;5236&quot;&gt;Extensive experience developing modern web applications using React or comparable front-end frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5237&quot; data-end=&quot;5336&quot;&gt;Strong expertise in relational and NoSQL database design, data modeling, and system architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5337&quot; data-end=&quot;5435&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience designing and delivering large-scale, production-ready software systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5436&quot; data-end=&quot;5523&quot;&gt;Experience leading complex technical initiatives spanning multiple projects or teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5524&quot; data-end=&quot;5614&quot;&gt;Strong software design, debugging, performance optimization, and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5615&quot; data-end=&quot;5669&quot;&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;5676&quot; data-end=&quot;5703&quot;&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;5705&quot; data-end=&quot;6363&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5705&quot; data-end=&quot;5845&quot;&gt;Experience building software platforms for manufacturing, industrial automation, robotics, aerospace, automotive, or defense environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5846&quot; data-end=&quot;5943&quot;&gt;Experience with cloud-native architectures, distributed systems, and event-driven applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;5944&quot; data-end=&quot;6018&quot;&gt;Experience with Kubernetes, Docker, and modern infrastructure platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6019&quot; data-end=&quot;6090&quot;&gt;Experience building CI/CD pipelines and automated testing frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6091&quot; data-end=&quot;6195&quot;&gt;Experience integrating enterprise systems such as ERP, PLM, MES, or manufacturing execution platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6196&quot; data-end=&quot;6290&quot;&gt;Demonstrated track record mentoring engineers and driving technical excellence across teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6291&quot; data-end=&quot;6363&quot;&gt;Experience influencing technical strategy and architectural direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;6370&quot; data-end=&quot;6389&quot;&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul data-start=&quot;6391&quot; data-end=&quot;6525&quot;&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6391&quot; data-end=&quot;6475&quot;&gt;This position is based onsite at Divergent&#39;s headquarters in Torrance, California.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li data-start=&quot;6476&quot; data-end=&quot;6525&quot;&gt;Expected onsite schedule is four days per week.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2 data-start=&quot;6532&quot; data-end=&quot;6547&quot;&gt;Compensation&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;6549&quot; data-end=&quot;6651&quot;&gt;This position is aligned to &lt;strong data-start=&quot;6577&quot; data-end=&quot;6602&quot;&gt;E05 – Senior Engineer&lt;/strong&gt; within Divergent&#39;s Engineering Career Framework.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p data-start=&quot;6653&quot; data-end=&quot;6699&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;6653&quot; data-end=&quot;6679&quot;&gt;E05 – Senior Engineer:&lt;/strong&gt; $141,380 – $194,390 + Equity&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$122,430&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$224,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
