&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Divergent is seeking an experienced and motivated analysis engineer to support the next generation of industry-leading vehicle development. We’re committed to transforming vehicles’ structural systems away from traditional manufacturing by using new materials and new technologies.&amp;nbsp; To do this, we need a forward-looking and innovative engineer who will help shape the future of industrial manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Structural Analyst &lt;/strong&gt;will build and manage FE models of structural components or full system architectures for a variety of vehicle platforms and perform detailed engineering analysis on structural components and systems using CAE programs. This position requires to work closely with inter-group engineers to understand manufacturing/design capabilities and limitations to ensure proposed design changes can be efficiently produced and assembled. Absorbing the latest technologies and collaborating successfully in a team environment is essential to ensure cross-functional requirements are met while achieving project targets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build up and analyze FE Models of Node™-based vehicle structures for aerospace flight applications or automotive use cases including validation using hand calculations and optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply cutting-edge FE/CAE methodology including nonlinear geometry / nonlinear material / implicit and explicit techniques to address complicated multi-physics problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Present technical analysis summary/reports efficiently at meetings and to other relevant engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create, refine, and execute new technical solutions for aerospace structures to support external customer programs and joint development efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work collaboratively in a team environment within the DAPS Product Engineering team and cross-functionally with other disciplines to efficiently design and release structures that are optimized for mass, efficient production, and assembly.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to implement cost reduction, methods and product improvements, and support prototype and production build activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BS in Mechanical / Aerospace Engineering with Minimum GPA of 3.2 or higher.&lt;/li&gt;
