&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Divergent, we are transforming how complex products—like performance vehicles and aerospace components—are designed, engineered, and manufactured. But our ability to scale isn’t just about technology. It’s about people.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re building a next-generation internal learning academy to rapidly onboard, upskill, and reskill a diverse workforce—ranging from hands-on technicians to world-class engineers. This isn’t a traditional training department; it’s a design lab for experiential learning at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re seeking a graduate-level Learning Architecture and Design Intern to help architect, prototype, and evaluate high-impact learning experiences grounded in adult learning principles, performance enablement, and human-centered design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instructional Design &amp;amp; Delivery&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Design and prototype learning modules and pathways for&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;advanced manufacturing technician and engineering roles &lt;/strong&gt;using adult learning and instructional design principles (e.g., experiential learning, microlearning, spaced repetition, and blended learning).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Experience Innovation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Explore how AI tutors, immersive simulations, and AR/VR environments can accelerate skill mastery and engagement across the workforce.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Curriculum Architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Partner with technical and operational leaders to translate job knowledge, skills and abilities and core values and behaviors into structured learning journeys and skill progression frameworks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning Evaluation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Develop and apply learning success metrics tied to real-world performance outcomes. Analyze data on engagement, skill transfer, and behavior change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Embed learning into our real-time feedback and capability-building systems—replacing static training with dynamic, in-flow development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Change &amp;amp; Communication Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Support adoption of new learning systems, tools, and rituals through targeted messaging and learner-centric enablement strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Applied Research&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Conduct focused research on adult learning, instructional design models, and technology-enhanced learning to inform continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to U.S. export controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Master’s or PhD candidate in Instructional Design, Learning Sciences, Adult &amp;amp; Continuing Education, or related field (Organizational Psychology or Behavioral Science welcome with strong learning design interest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing learning materials, programs, or experiences (academic, professional, or applied)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity analyzing complex datasets to identify trends, patterns, and insights that support business decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating reports and presentations that effectively communicate data-driven findings and recommendations to non-technical stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable using AI tools to support writing, content creation, research, and workflow efficiency.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of adult learning theory, curriculum design, and instructional models&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong research and synthesis skills—able to translate insights into actionable learning strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth mindset and eagerness to learn through feedback&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and visual communication skills along with a strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of success in fast-paced, experimental, high-autonomy environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to learning design or authoring tools (Articulate, Captivate, Rise, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with LMS environments and standards such as SCORM or xAPI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to learning technologies leveraging AI, AR/VR, or simulation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with job task analysis, skills mapping, or competency frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort analyzing engagement and learning data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience in instructional design, L&amp;amp;D, or workforce development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity about AI, emerging technology, and the future of work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Why This Internship?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This isn’t a typical HR or training internship—it’s an opportunity to design the future of learning in advanced manufacturing. You’ll help craft scalable, high-impact learning systems that empower technicians, engineers, and leaders to grow fast and perform at their peak.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll prototype modern learning experiences—from adaptive simulations to AI-powered feedback loops—transforming how people learn and perform in a high-innovation environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
