&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$37&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$40 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Equal Employment Opportunity&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Divergent is an Equal Opportunity Employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age, disability or veteran status, or any other applicable state or federal protected characteristic. Divergent provides affirmative action in employment for qualified Individuals with Disabilities and Protected Veterans in compliance with Section 503 of the Rehabilitation Act and the Vietnam Era Veterans’ Readjustment Assistance Act.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.eeoc.gov/sites/default/files/2023-06/22-088_EEOC_KnowYourRights6.12.pdf&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;EEO Poster&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a highly motivated and hands-on Inspection &amp;amp; Metrology Supervisor to lead daily inspection and measurement activities across production and development environments. This role is critical to ensuring product quality, compliance, and data integrity through robust inspection processes and strong technical leadership. The ideal candidate is a working leader with deep metrology expertise, strong people skills, and the ability to drive consistency, accountability, and continuous improvement within a fast-paced manufacturing environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supervise daily inspection and metrology operations, including CMMs, portable arms, laser/structured-light scanning, and conventional inspection methods.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support a team of inspection and metrology technicians, ensuring adherence to quality standards, inspection plans, and production schedules.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the technical point of contact for measurement strategy, CMM execution, and inspection troubleshooting on the production floor.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure CMM programs and inspection methods are executed in a repeatable, efficient manner; partner with engineering to improve cycle time and robustness.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate workload, staffing, and equipment utilization to support short- and long-term production and program needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Manufacturing Engineering, Quality Engineering, and Production teams to resolve inspection issues, support RCCAs, and improve manufacturability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive adherence to quality systems, customer requirements, and internal standards (ISO, AS, drawing requirements, control plans).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review inspection results, identify trends, and escalate quality risks; support containment and corrective actions as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment of new metrology technologies, automation efforts, and fixturing solutions to improve repeatability and throughput.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coach, train, and mentor technicians on GD&amp;amp;T interpretation, inspection techniques, reporting standards, and best practices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure accurate documentation of inspection activities, nonconformances, and measurement records.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote a culture of quality ownership, continuous improvement, safety, and clear communication within the team and across the factory.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain an organized, efficient inspection environment aligned with 5S and lean manufacturing principles.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of hands-on experience with inspection, metrology, and quality within a fast-paced aerospace/automotive manufacturing or production environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience in a people leadership or supervisory role, with direct responsibility for coaching and performance management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of metrology operations and programming (PC-DMIS, Calypso, Zeiss inspect, verisurf, or equivalent), including execution in high-mix production.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in GD&amp;amp;T with the ability to interpret complex engineering drawings and translate them into effective inspection strategies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with a variety of metrology &amp;amp; inspection tools, including CMMs, portable arms, laser/structured-light scanners, &amp;amp; conventional precision instruments (manual inspection, borescopes, comparators, etc).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting skills to diagnose and resolve inspection, measurement, or data integrity issues quickly.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working on the production floor and supporting technicians hands-on as needed.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills; able to interface effectively with engineering, production, and quality teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within regulated quality systems (ISO, AS, or customer-specific requirements).&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage changing priorities in a fast-paced engineering and production environment.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW206226875 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW206226875 BCX8&quot;&gt;Hands-on experience with metrology, such as laser scanning or structured light measurement&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW206226875 BCX8&quot;&gt;, CMMs, &amp;amp; scan arms&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW206226875 BCX8&quot;&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW206226875 BCX8&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:259}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience interfacing CMM data with manufacturing execution systems (MES) or statistical process control (SPC) software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a Machine Shop&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with design for manufacture and product development life cycle&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with quality tools including root cause and corrective action, QMS and process auditing and statistical analysis of quality metrics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
