&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;In order to adjust to changes in our business, it may become necessary to add, remove or modify certain duties and responsibilities, or to reassign you to another job position. From time to time you may be asked to work on special projects or to assist with other work. Your cooperation and assistance in performing such additional work is expected.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;E-Verify: Right to Work&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Our company participates in &lt;a href=&quot;https://e-verify.uscis.gov/web/media/resourcesContents/E-Verify_Participation_Poster_ES.pdf&quot;&gt;E-Verify&lt;/a&gt;. E-Verify is a program that electronically confirms a candidate’s eligibility to work in the United States after completing the Employment Eligibility Verification (Form I-9). The information provided on the Form I-9 is compared to the records contained in the Social Security Administration and Department of Homeland Security (DHS) databases. This helps employers verify the identity and employment eligibility of newly hired employees.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/IER_RightToWorkPoster.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (English)&lt;/a&gt; |&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.e-verify.gov/sites/default/files/everify/posters/IER_RighttoWorkPosterES.pdf&quot;&gt;Eligibility to Work Poster (Spanish)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO)&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Pursuant to the Los Angeles Fair Chance Initiative for Hiring Ordinance (FCIHO), we will consider for employment qualified applicants with arrest and conviction records.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;No agencies, no solicitations, and no calls please.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Divergent is seeking a &lt;strong&gt;Teamcenter PLM Solution Architect&lt;/strong&gt; to lead the architecture, design, and evolution of our Siemens Teamcenter PLM ecosystem. This individual will serve as a technical leader responsible for designing scalable PLM solutions that enable engineering, manufacturing, and enterprise teams to collaborate efficiently throughout the product lifecycle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work closely with engineering, manufacturing, IT, and business stakeholders to expand Teamcenter capabilities, integrate enterprise systems, improve user experiences, and deliver high-impact PLM solutions supporting some of the most advanced manufacturing technologies in the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to own the technical direction of a mission-critical PLM platform while helping shape the future of next-generation manufacturing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&amp;nbsp;will be part of a team that handles support of Teamcenter, NX, and Easy Plan. The primary responsibilities are designing and building new applications, enhancing the systems, and assisting end users. Additionally, you will work with our application teams to help with system administration, implement workflows, integrate systems, provide consulting help, and provide general expertise on Teamcenter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a key resource for investigating, analyzing, and designing new applications and functionality for our Teamcenter and NX environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help define and evolve the overall architecture for our Siemens Teamcenter PLM environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design scalable, maintainable, and high-performance PLM solutions that support engineering, manufacturing, and enterprise business processes. Applications can include ITK, SOA, OData based stand-alone applications, or extensions to Teamcenter and NX themselves.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design extensions to the Teamcenter object model to support integrations and data sharing between NX, ERP, and MES systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customize the Active Workspace, streamline the user interface, and add new functionality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate new Teamcenter and NX capabilities and recommend technology improvements that increase scalability, usability, and add value to our Engineering user base.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design new and enhance existing workflows to support both Change Management and Release Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with users to gather requirements and design new features and functionality for the system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Author project definition and design documents for various enterprise level projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consult with various departments on best practices and to trouble shoot problems and issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering, IT, and manufacturing stakeholders to continuously improve PLM adoption and usability&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Basic Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lawfully access information and technology that is subject to US export controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience working with Teamcenter implementations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with the Teamcenter BMIDE, Classification, Workflows, Change Management, NX integration, the Rich Client, the Active Workspace, and customization of the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with the ITK and SOA APIs. Experience with the OData interface is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience programming in C++, C#, Java, and/or Python.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of PLM concepts, including product structures, configuration management, workflows, and lifecycle management.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience creating workflows and with Teamcenter Change Management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong troubleshooting and problem-solving skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills, and the ability to support both technical and non-technical users.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with data migrations, upgrades, and multi-site environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a manufacturing or high-growth technology business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Teamcenter Cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Easy Plan, Opcenter and Mendix.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with NX, NX Manager, and customizing NX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience installing and upgrading Teamcenter and NX.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Work Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Onsite/Hybrid preferred, open to remote&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Pay Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$163,270&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$224,500 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Holistic Compensation Package:&lt;/strong&gt; Enjoy a world-class compensation package that includes a competitive salary, equity plan, and discretionary results-based incentive bonus opportunities, ensuring you&#39;re truly valued for your contributions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Wellness and Time Off: &lt;/strong&gt;Embrace a healthy lifestyle with paid vacation, sick time, and company holidays, including a year-end shutdown to recharge. We support growing families with paid parental leave, recognizing the importance of bonding time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Comprehensive Health and Wellness: &lt;/strong&gt;Prioritize your well-being with our comprehensive health and wellness benefits, offering both HMO and Premium PPO options. Additionally, benefit from company-sponsored life insurance and short and long-term disability coverage for peace of mind.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Investment in Growth:&lt;/strong&gt; We&#39;re committed to your professional development. Take advantage of reimbursement opportunities for learning and development initiatives, empowering you to continuously expand your skill set and reach peak performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and High-Performing Environment:&lt;/strong&gt; Join our collaborative, dynamic, and high-performing team within a fast-paced, mission-driven company. Together, we&#39;re disrupting the traditional manufacturing industry, fostering innovation, and integrating people and technology to reduce our footprint.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
