&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Divergent is building the new industrial age. Every day, our teams design, manufacture, and assemble advanced systems for some of the world’s most demanding industries. Our integrated engineering and manufacturing platform transforms complex designs into production-ready solutions, helping customers move faster, build smarter, and deliver critical systems when they matter most. Divergent is a qualified Tier 1 supplier to global automotive OEMs and supports leading U.S. aerospace and defense companies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join us and help push the boundaries of what can be built.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;Purpose&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Divergent Technologies is seeking a Vice President, Washington Operations to lead the strategic development of the company&#39;s newly formed Washington, DC / Northern Virginia office. Working at the intersection of business and government, the Vice President serves as Divergent&#39;s primary liaison to the Department of War and other Executive Branch agencies. This executive leads strategic engagements to advance Divergent&#39;s interests and, in particular, to identify, shape, and support the capture of business development and other strategic opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;The Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Washington Office Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent Divergent as a senior, visible presence in the Washington defense and aerospace community, including the shaping and influence of business development and other strategic opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in establishing and leading the Washington, DC / Northern Virginia office, including its strategy, operating model, staffing plan, budget, and performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in recruitment, development, and leadership of a high-caliber team of government relations, policy, and business development professionals as the office grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Government Liaison and Strategic Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the principal point of contact with the Department of War, the Military Departments, defense agencies, and other Executive Branch agencies, and the connective tissue between those stakeholders and the congressional defense committees&#39; professional staff, as well as industry partners, think tanks, and trade associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and sustain trusted relationships with senior acquisition, requirements, technology, and industrial base leaders and decision makers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead strategic engagements to position Divergent as a preferred partner for advanced manufacturing and defense industrial base priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
